    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Africa and register",
     "texto": [
      "**Bué** (very, a lot) comes from the speech of Luanda and has spread to informal youth speech in Portugal. It can intensify an adjective (**está bué bom**) or appear in **bué de + noun**; its frequency and construction vary by community and register. It isn't a neutral form for every context."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Other vocabulary",
     "texto": [
      "In Mozambique **chapa** is used for a minibus. It's best to learn these words in context, because they change from one neighbourhood to another."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
